fact WorkItem(id: "WI-172", description: some(value: "scaland mirror of WI-030 — SLD O(n²) optimization: lazy substitution in resolve/SearchStream.scala. stepChoicePoint had been eagerly walking every remaining goal applying the new substitution after each match: SearchStream.scala:191 (after a ground-fact match) and :206 (after a rule-body match). Fix: drop the eager applySubst-each from both paths; walk goals(0) lazily through frame.subst at goal-selection time in stepInit; memoize the walked form back into goals(0) so choice-point retries don't re-walk; skip the structural walk when σ is empty. Reduces O(n²) over the goal list to O(n × goal_size). Also fixed latent shape mismatch in Builtins.executeExtractSort surfaced by lazy walking — emit canonical nullary Fn shape (kb.makeNameTermFromSym) instead of Term.Ref(functor); pre-fix the eager apply silently overwrote the inconsistency. Added ResolveStats telemetry (steps, lazyWalkCalls), exposed via SearchStream.stats. Tests: smoke at n=50; acceptance asserts lazyWalkCalls < 8·n at n=400 and ratio < 6× between n=100 and n=400 (quadratic gives ~16×). Files: scaland/core/src/main/scala/anthill/{subst/Substitution,resolve/SearchStream,resolve/Builtins}.scala; scaland/core/src/test/scala/anthill/resolve/ResolveTest.scala (+2 tests + n-body fixture). Acceptance: sbt test green (122 tests)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-04T05:11:52Z"))
